    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs could personalize explanations (e.g., breaking down calculus proofs interactively) or generate adaptive quizzes. They could bridge gaps too: e.g., flaging misconceptions early in physics/economics (where I struggle). For a student like me, a hybrid approach—AI for explanations + peer teaching—might feel less overwhelming than dry textbooks."
